{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>והאיש מִשְתָּאֵה</b> — like 'astounded,' from the root of 'שאו ערים' (Isaiah 6:11), 'תשאה שממה' (ibid.)." "And 'לה' means 'for her sake,' and likewise 'אשתומם כשעה חדא' (Daniel 4:16), and the tav is of the hitpa'el pattern, like 'נתראה פנים' (2 Kings 14:8), and it is impossible that it be from שתה."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:36.250328898Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}